Summary: Hometown Knight makes good, becomes local hero
Keywords: Possible Spoilers

Well, he wasn't particularly elegant about it, but my amazing Knight
bashed his way through all the levels and eventually ascended.

I scarcely used my magic marker at all (I think I may have made one
enchant armor scroll) which meant that I lugged around all those blank
scrolls for nothing.

I also carried around a lot of extra holy water.  I didn't even notice
that my luckstone was cursed by the end.
(Oops -- fortunately it didn't matter too much)

Another mistake was losing the Magic Mirror of Merlin along the way
somewhere.  I saw the Wiz steal it, but it either wasn't with his corpse
or I simply forgot to take it somehow.

I first tried bashing the Wiz, then got fed up and hit him with a Wand of
Death.  Ironically, I used this on the earlier incarnations, and just
hacked his later versions to death with my +6 Excalibur.

The Elemental Plane of Air was a bit tricky.  I tried polymorphing
into flying things like mind flayers and vampire lords, but a few
spin cycles in an elemental can do a lot of damage.  I eventually got
wounded enough that I decided to swap the Amulet of Yendor for one
of life saving temporarily.  During the whole game, however, I never used
any of my 7 amulets of life saving.

I was lucky to eventually stumble my way out of the Elemental Plane of Water.
I "found" the portal once, without actually seeing it, then lost it again
in the chaos of fighting monsters.  I forgot that the Water plane has
that weird drifting effect.  When I eventually located it, it was under
a corpse.  Sigh.

Finally, on the Astral Plane, I unfortunately screwed up by entering
with a ring of Conflict on.  Then I stumbled about blindly (I was blind
for almost all of the time for whatever reason) and went to BOTH of the
incorrect altars first.  Sigh.  Crawl Crawl Stagger Stagger...

When I eventually made it to the correct altar, I still had a
wand of wishing (1).  I used that charge to get 3 crystals, and didn't
bother trying to wrest out the last one.  I also never bothered to
polypile gems or anything to try to improve my score, as I was just set
on getting the heck out of there :)

I killed Juiblex (2 times)	Was he wearing an AOLS when I hacked out?

Finally, this game was free of the Utterly_Stupid_Mistakes(tm)
which had killed off two previous contenders for the throne.

